/* --- Instellingen · Vanzelf stoppen: accu en temperatuur --- */
"stop.accu.titel" = "On a nearly empty battery";
"stop.accu.onder" = "Stop below";
"stop.accu.uitleg" = "Working without a charger, the Mac may sleep again as soon as the battery drops below this level. Without that floor the battery simply runs all the way down with the lid closed. You are not asked for your password for this.";
"stop.warm.titel" = "When the Mac gets too warm";
"stop.warm.uitleg" = "This happens by itself and cannot be switched off. If the Mac gets critically warm, Dopamine Code stops immediately so macOS can step in again. At \"high\" you only get a warning.";
"stop.waarom.titel" = "Why you cannot switch these three off";
"stop.waarom.uitleg" = "To keep the Mac awake with the lid closed, Dopamine Code has to flip one system setting: the sleep block (SleepDisabled). That same setting also disables macOS's emergency brake — the automatic sleep on a nearly empty battery and on overheating. The time limit, the battery floor and the temperature watch above take that job over. That is why they are always part of it.";

