"aan.app.geendraaiend" = "No running apps found";
"aan.app.uitleg" = "The list shows what is running now; what you pick is stored by name and applies next time too. Keeping awake switches on as soon as such an app starts — if it is already running when you pick it, nothing happens until it starts again. The session stops once that app has finished, by exactly the same route as \"dopamine on --until-exit\".";

/* --- Instellingen · Zelf aanzetten: klep en vangnetten --- */
"aan.klep.titel" = "As soon as you close the lid";
"aan.klep.uitleg" = "This lives in the menu bar panel and not here, because it applies once: you click \"Turn on when I close the lid\", you close it, and keeping awake switches on. If you do not, it expires by itself after five minutes and the app says so. It deliberately does not survive a restart: nobody expects something armed hours ago to still go off.";
"aan.omheen.titel" = "What stays wrapped around it regardless";
"aan.omheen.uitleg" = "Everything that switches on by itself here takes exactly the same route as the switch: the same time limit, the same battery floor and the same temperature watch. If it cannot be switched on safely at that moment — the battery too low, the Mac too warm, or the password exemption gone — nothing happens, and you get a notification about it. A schedule never runs longer than the time limit: set that to 4 hours with the window until 18:00, and it stops at 13:00 and not at 18:00. And within one window the schedule fires at most once, even if something stopped in between — otherwise the schedule would put back what a safety net had just released.";
